WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.777 --> 00:00:15.600
Zann through a small cavern and into another tunnel.

2
00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:19.881
"I think the intersection is just ahead," he whispered to Zing.

3
00:00:20.661 --> 00:00:25.482
Zing breathed out a small flame, allowing Zann to see a little farther than the crawler's feeble glow

4
00:00:25.522 --> 00:00:29.163
permitted. There was no intersection—just a blank stone wall.

5
00:00:29.183 --> 00:00:31.184
"Drat," Zann muttered.

6
00:00:32.204 --> 00:00:34.225
He retraced his steps and tried a different tunnel.

7
00:00:34.885 --> 00:00:37.766
Why hadn't he paid more attention when Tok was leading them out earlier?

8
00:00:37.786 --> 00:00:40.406
"Never mind," Zann whispered.

9
00:00:40.726 --> 00:00:42.787
At least he'd managed to sneak away undetected.

10
00:00:43.647 --> 00:00:44.307
Or had he?

11
00:00:44.747 --> 00:00:47.848
Zann froze as he heard a soft scraping sound behind him.

12
00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:51.409
It echoed down the tunnel, barely louder than a heartbeat.

13
00:00:51.429 --> 00:00:52.930
"Did you hear that?"

14
00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:54.130
he whispered to Zing.

15
00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:57.131
But apparently Zing hadn't heard the sound.

16
00:00:57.791 --> 00:01:00.392
The dragon was staring at Zann's crawler hungrily.

17
00:01:01.172 --> 00:01:01.852
Zann sighed.

18
00:01:02.156 --> 00:01:04.237
Being in the creepy cave was making him jumpy.

19
00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:09.800
The sound had probably been nothing more than a cave creature or a stray burst of magic energy.

20
00:01:10.601 --> 00:01:13.462
Zann kept moving, watching for anything that looked familiar.

21
00:01:14.223 --> 00:01:15.644
Clink! Zann froze.

22
00:01:16.284 --> 00:01:17.024
Was that a footstep?

23
00:01:17.044 --> 00:01:22.227
"Quiet!" he hissed, dragging Zing into a crevasse in the wall.

24
00:01:22.948 --> 00:01:26.049
He pressed both hands over his crawler, trying to block its light.

25
00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:30.592
Zing's breath felt hot on Zann's leg, but Zann didn't dare move.

26
00:01:31.296 --> 00:01:32.517
The footsteps came closer.

27
00:01:32.897 --> 00:01:34.998
Soon Zann could hear the sound of breathing.

28
00:01:35.778 --> 00:01:38.179
He pressed himself back against the stone and watched.

29
00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:43.862
A figure passed, lit only by the soft glow of the crawler perched on its shoulder.

30
00:01:43.882 --> 00:01:46.723
"Perda!" Zann blurted out.

31
00:01:47.483 --> 00:01:49.604
Perda jumped in surprise and spun to face him.

32
00:01:49.624 --> 00:01:52.526
"Zann! I was afraid I'd lost you."

33
00:01:53.326 --> 00:01:53.986
Zann frowned.

34
00:01:54.427 --> 00:01:55.587
"You were following me?"

35
00:01:55.607 --> 00:01:57.008
"Of course."

36
00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:58.021
Perda laughed.

37
00:01:59.682 --> 00:02:03.645
"You didn't think you could sneak off and have another adventure without me, did you?"

38
00:02:03.665 --> 00:02:07.808
"But I was sure nobody saw me leave," said Zann.

39
00:02:07.828 --> 00:02:09.069
"You're right.

40
00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:11.451
I didn't notice you were gone for a few minutes.

41
00:02:12.312 --> 00:02:13.993
I used my crawler to track you."

42
00:02:14.654 --> 00:02:17.896
Perda pointed to her crawler, which was keeping a wary eye on Zing.

43
00:02:17.916 --> 00:02:22.300
"I'd already noticed it gets more and more nervous the closer we are to Zing.

44
00:02:23.044 --> 00:02:27.868
All I had to do was pay attention to how deeply its claws were digging into my shoulder

45
00:02:27.968 --> 00:02:29.249
to guess how close you were."

46
00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:31.511
Zann rolled his eyes.

47
00:02:31.831 --> 00:02:34.493
At the same time, he had to admire Perda's cleverness.

48
00:02:34.513 --> 00:02:37.236
"You have to go back," he told her.

49
00:02:37.256 --> 00:02:38.597
"It's too risky.

50
00:02:39.357 --> 00:02:44.161
Besides, maybe you can figure out a way to delay the Sealing spell until I'm finished."

51
00:02:44.181 --> 00:02:46.963
"Don't worry about that," Perda said.

52
00:02:46.983 --> 00:02:49.705
"The adults will be arguing for a while yet.

53
00:02:50.466 --> 00:02:52.668
Venna showed up right after you disappeared.

54
00:02:53.456 --> 00:02:55.037
She admitted to taking the relics.

55
00:02:55.878 --> 00:02:56.858
Most of them anyway."

56
00:02:58.019 --> 00:02:58.980
Zann was stunned.

57
00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.701
"Venna took the relics?

58
00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:05.704
Why?" "She doesn't think it's right to seal off the Cave and all the powerful magic in the

59
00:03:05.764 --> 00:03:09.827
relics. She thinks we should take some of the relics back to First City.

60
00:03:10.548 --> 00:03:15.171
That way the Red Council can use them in case a threat like Morb ever comes along again."

61
00:03:15.191 --> 00:03:18.733
"Wow." Zann knew how persuasive Venna could be.

62
00:03:18.753 --> 00:03:20.814
"Does anyone agree with her?"

63
00:03:20.834 --> 00:03:22.836
"A few people."

64
00:03:23.128 --> 00:03:23.768
Perda shrugged.

65
00:03:23.788 --> 00:03:25.889
"Not Boz and Teplo, though.

66
00:03:26.189 --> 00:03:28.970
They'll all be arguing about it for a long time."

67
00:03:28.990 --> 00:03:30.890
"Good," Zann said.

68
00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:33.951
"That will give me enough time to find the message chamber."

69
00:03:34.751 --> 00:03:38.372
"You mean it'll give us enough time," Perda said.

70
00:03:38.392 --> 00:03:41.513
"If you don't let me come, you'll never get there.

71
00:03:42.193 --> 00:03:44.734
You've been going the wrong way for the past ten minutes.

72
00:03:45.754 --> 00:03:48.115
Fortunately I remember how to get there.

73
00:03:48.255 --> 00:03:49.155
It's back this way."

74
00:03:49.876 --> 00:03:51.316
Perda quickly headed down the tunnel.

75
00:03:52.348 --> 00:03:53.589
Zann hurried to keep up with her.

76
00:03:53.949 --> 00:03:55.570
He was still annoyed that she'd followed him.

77
00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:58.251
But another part of him was glad to have her help.

78
00:03:59.011 --> 00:04:01.592
Half an hour later, they stepped into the message chamber.

79
00:04:01.612 --> 00:04:03.573
"Hurry," Perda urged.

80
00:04:03.593 --> 00:04:06.914
"Who knows how long we have until they start the Sealing spell.

81
00:04:07.615 --> 00:04:09.275
Then we'll be trapped in here forever."

82
00:04:10.276 --> 00:04:12.317
Zann’s stone was still burning hot.

83
00:04:13.117 --> 00:04:15.818
He took a deep breath and plugged it into the wall.

84
00:04:15.838 --> 00:04:20.000
"Oh!" he gasped as two figures appeared before him.

85
00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:21.901
"Is that your parents?"

86
00:04:22.301 --> 00:04:22.961
Perda whispered.

87
00:04:23.782 --> 00:04:25.703
Zann just nodded, taking in the sight.

88
00:04:25.723 --> 00:04:29.245
"Greetings, Wyssa," his father's familiar voice said.

89
00:04:29.265 --> 00:04:31.606
"We received your last message."

90
00:04:31.626 --> 00:04:35.308
"We accept your terms," Zann's mother added.

91
00:04:35.328 --> 00:04:38.430
"We're very eager to locate World X.

92
00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:42.512
If you're sure you can lead us there, we'll pay your fee."

93
00:04:43.292 --> 00:04:44.293
Zann's father nodded.

94
00:04:44.673 --> 00:04:49.396
"We've just returned from the Cave of the Unknown and have one more short trip to make.

95
00:04:50.124 --> 00:04:51.704
We'll contact you when we return."

96
00:04:52.485 --> 00:04:54.765
Zann was so overwhelmed he could barely move.

97
00:04:55.505 --> 00:04:58.186
His parents' holograms flickered out and then reappeared.

98
00:04:58.206 --> 00:05:01.627
"Greetings, Wyssa the message began again.

99
00:05:01.647 --> 00:05:03.968
"Wow," Perda said.

100
00:05:03.988 --> 00:05:06.949
"I—ouch!" She poked her crawler.

101
00:05:07.309 --> 00:05:07.969
It was trembling.

102
00:05:08.849 --> 00:05:12.010
Zann realized his own crawler was digging its claws into his shoulder.

103
00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:14.591
"What's the matter with the crawlers?"

104
00:05:14.971 --> 00:05:16.851
he mumbled, still watching his parents.

105
00:05:17.711 --> 00:05:19.732
"They seem nervous," said Perda.

106
00:05:20.044 --> 00:05:22.505
"And Zing isn't even trying to eat them right now."

107
00:05:23.445 --> 00:05:25.105
The entire chamber shuddered.

108
00:05:25.906 --> 00:05:29.267
The message stone popped out of the wall, cutting off the hologram.

109
00:05:29.287 --> 00:05:31.287
"Uh-oh," Perda said.

110
00:05:31.307 --> 00:05:32.508
"Did you feel that?

111
00:05:33.228 --> 00:05:35.888
The Magic Masters must be starting the Sealing spell.

112
00:05:36.609 --> 00:05:38.029
We have to get out of here!"

113
00:05:38.849 --> 00:05:39.950
Zann didn't want to leave.

114
00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:44.651
He wanted to plug the stone back in and watch his parents' message again and again.

115
00:05:44.671 --> 00:05:46.651
There was another rumble.

116
00:05:47.452 --> 00:05:48.392
Zing let out a squeak.

117
00:05:49.044 --> 00:05:50.786
Zann's crawler moaned with fear.

118
00:05:50.806 --> 00:05:53.608
"Okay, let's go," Zann said.

119
00:05:54.409 --> 00:05:57.111
With Zing flying ahead of her, Perda ran for the exit.

120
00:05:57.832 --> 00:05:58.913
Zann started to follow.

121
00:05:59.653 --> 00:06:00.854
Suddenly he paused.

122
00:06:01.235 --> 00:06:04.537
Turning, he raced over and grabbed the message stone off the floor.

123
00:06:05.298 --> 00:06:07.020
Then he sprinted after Zing and Perda.
